<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43337" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐά̆γωγ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>easily led, ductile</i>,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπί τι, εἴς τι, τινι πρός
			τι</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				486d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Oec.</u>
				12.15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1327b38
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς πᾶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					11.29.9
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς ἀκολασίαν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.E.
					<u>M.</u>
					6.34
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span>
			<i>by</i> a master, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Lg.</u>
				671b
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλισ-οτέρα ὑπὸ τῶν τυχόντων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					<u>Ep.</u>
					2.15
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐάγωγόν ἐστι πᾶς ἀνὴρ ἐρῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Men.
					352
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>easily purged</i>, -
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ότατος χυμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					15.78
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<i>easily managed</i>, of the Nile, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				11.13
			</span></i>; of horses, <i>docile</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				1.195
			</span></i>; of the voice, <i>easily trained</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.117
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δακτύλων τὸ εὐ.</span>, of a
			statue, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Im.</u>
				6
			</span></i>; of land, <i>easily cultivated</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				5.3.12
			</span></i>; <i>commodious</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐνδιαιτήσεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					1.334
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γως</span>
			<i>in an accommodating spirit</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Cic.
				<u>Att.</u>
				13.23.3
			</span></i>.</div>
